# Rust build output
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Compiled Zed extension component. This is a build artifact: Zed (dev-install)
# and the zed-industries/extensions registry both compile + componentize the
# extension from source, so the .wasm is never consumed from git. Committing it
# only caused version drift. See https://zed.dev/blog/zed-decoded-extensions
extension/extension.wasm

# Grammar sources Zed checks out and compiles when it (re)builds this as a dev
# extension: it clones each `[grammars.*]` repository into `extension/grammars/<name>`
# (full working copies, each with its own .git) and caches the compiled .wasm beside
# them. Pure build output — the pinned rev in extension.toml is the source of truth,
# and the registry does the same checkout on its own machines.
extension/grammars/

# Node modules (webview-src)
preview-binary/webview-src/node_modules/
preview-binary/webview-src/dist/
preview-binary/webview-src/.vite/

# Vite build output embedded into the binary at compile time (index.html, the
# JS/CSS bundle under assets/, and the copied drawing fonts). All of it is
# regenerated by `vite build` (`just ui`) — CI runs that before cargo — so none
# of it belongs in git. A bare `cargo build` of the binary now requires the UI
# to have been built first (just ui / just build / just release / install-locally).
preview-binary/assets/

# Lock files
preview-binary/Cargo.lock

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claudine/tmp/
